-- Tests for the Chapter 25.1 critical safety incident encoding, with expected values
-- written by hand from the source text and a calendar. The day-counting for every date
-- is in NOTES.md ("How the expected dates were worked out"); none was copied from l4's
-- output.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
-- Every assertion here is expected to be satisfied. A failure is a finding.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tfaia-domain`
IMPORT `tfaia-definitions`
IMPORT `tfaia-reporting`
IMPORT `tfaia-penalty`
IMPORT `tfaia-seat`

-- The YMD shim: the stable prelude has no YMD (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md, section 5).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

§ `Fixtures`

`ten to the 26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000000
`just over ten to the 26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000001
`twice ten to the 26` MEANS 200000000000000000000000000
`half ten to the 26` MEANS 50000000000000000000000000

-- Developer and model, fields in order: AI model, broad data set, generality, adaptable,
-- trained it, operations used so far, most operations on any foundation model, revenue.
`a large developer's frontier model`   MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 600000000
`a smaller developer's frontier model` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000000
`someone else's frontier model`        MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 600000000
`my smaller foundation model`          MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `half ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 600000000
`a model of a developer below the line` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `half ten to the 26` `half ten to the 26` 600000000

`no model conduct` MEANS `none of the three kinds of conduct`
`CBRN assistance` MEANS `provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon`

-- Incidents, fields in order: weights compromised, weights harm, conduct, materially
-- contributed, single incident, people, dollars, public information, lawful federal
-- activity, loss of control, loss-of-control harm, deception, in an evaluation,
-- materially increased risk.
`nothing happened`                MEANS `the incident` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a weights theft that injured`    MEANS `the incident` TRUE TRUE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a weights theft that injured no one` MEANS `the incident` TRUE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a loss of control that killed`   MEANS `the incident` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a loss of control that harmed no one` MEANS `the incident` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a theft and a loss of control`   MEANS `the incident` TRUE TRUE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN people IS A NUMBER, dollars IS A NUMBER, public IS A BOOLEAN, federal IS A BOOLEAN, mc IS A BOOLEAN, single IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `what the model did`
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`a catastrophe` people dollars public federal mc single c MEANS
    `the incident` FALSE FALSE c mc single people dollars public federal FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN eval IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`a deception` eval risk MEANS
    `the incident` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE eval risk

-- Position, fields in order: day of discovery, imminent risk, federal route declared,
-- chapter in force, federal-contract conflict.
`discovered 2 March 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 3 2
`plainly`        MEANS `the position` `discovered 2 March 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`imminently`     MEANS `the position` `discovered 2 March 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`by the federal route` MEANS `the position` `discovered 2 March 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`out of force`   MEANS `the position` `discovered 2 March 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`under a federal contract` MEANS `the position` `discovered 2 March 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`discovered 31 December 2025` MEANS `the position` (YMD 2025 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`discovered 1 January 2026`   MEANS `the position` (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

`no other holidays` MEANS LIST

§ `Section 22757.11: who is a frontier developer, and a large one`

-- Exactly 10^26 operations is not "greater than" 10^26; one more is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 `ten to the 26`))
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 `just over ten to the 26`
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `twice ten to the 26`
-- A model that is not a foundation model (not adaptable; not an AI model), with no
-- other foundation model over the line. (These two first gave 'most operations on any
-- foundation model' as 2 x 10^26, which by that input's own @desc says another
-- foundation model is over the line; the inputs were corrected, not the expectation.)
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` 0))
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `just over ten to the 26` 0
#ASSERT (NOT (`the model is a frontier model` (`the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 0)))
#ASSERT `the model is a frontier model` (`the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `just over ten to the 26` 0 0)
#ASSERT (NOT (`the model is a frontier model` `my smaller foundation model`))
#ASSERT `I am a frontier developer` `my smaller foundation model`

-- "in excess of five hundred million dollars": exactly $500,000,000 is not large.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000000))
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000001
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 `ten to the 26` 900000000000))

§ `Section 22757.11(c), (d): critical safety incidents`

#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` `nothing happened`))
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured`
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured no one`))
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` `a loss of control that killed`
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` `a loss of control that harmed no one`))
-- The same event with a model that is not a frontier model is no critical safety incident.
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `my smaller foundation model` `a loss of control that killed`))
-- Someone else's frontier model: still a critical safety incident (the definition says "a frontier model").
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `someone else's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured`

-- Kind 2: more than 50 people, or more than $1,000,000,000, and the exclusions.
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `CBRN assistance`)
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 50 1000000000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `CBRN assistance`)))
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 0 1000000001 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `evaded the control of its frontier developer or user`)
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `CBRN assistance`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `CBRN assistance`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `CBRN assistance`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `CBRN assistance`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a catastrophe` 51 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no model conduct`)))

-- Kind 4: outside an evaluation designed to elicit it, and demonstrating materially increased risk.
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a deception` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a deception` TRUE TRUE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large developer's frontier model` (`a deception` FALSE FALSE)))

-- Kinds overlap; both are listed.
#ASSERT `the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` `a large developer's frontier model` `a theft and a loss of control` EQUALS LIST `kind 1, unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury`, `kind 3, loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury`
#ASSERT `the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` `my smaller foundation model` `a theft and a loss of control` EQUALS LIST

-- Through the exported question.
#ASSERT `is this a critical safety incident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`is this a critical safety incident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ten to the 26` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `Section 22757.13(c)(1): the 15-day report`

-- Discovered Monday 2 March 2026: the 15th day is Tuesday 17 March.
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 3 17, YMD 2026 3 17
-- Every frontier developer, large or not.
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a smaller developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 3 17, YMD 2026 3 17
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a model of a developer below the line` `a weights theft that injured` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `no duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `someone else's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `no duty, because the model is not a frontier model of mine`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `my smaller foundation model` `a loss of control that killed` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `not required but encouraged, because the model is a foundation model of mine that is not a frontier model`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `my smaller foundation model` `nothing happened` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `no duty, because the model is not a frontier model of mine`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `nothing happened` `plainly` `no other holidays` EQUALS `no duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `by the federal route` `no other holidays` EQUALS `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the chapter`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `out of force` `no other holidays` EQUALS `not covered, because I have said the chapter is not in force, or is preempted, as applied to me`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `under a federal contract` `no other holidays` EQUALS `not covered, because a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the reporting duty`
-- The chapter took effect 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `discovered 31 December 2025` `no other holidays` EQUALS `not covered, because I discovered the incident before the chapter took effect on 1 January 2026`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `discovered 1 January 2026` `no other holidays` EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 1 16, YMD 2026 1 16

-- Holidays (Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12a, 135; Gov. Code § 6700(a)(1)): Saturdays and Sundays
-- are holidays without being listed. Discovered Friday 6 March 2026: the 15th day is
-- Saturday 21 March, Sunday 22 March is a holiday too, so Monday 23 March. Listing the
-- Sunday as well is harmless. (Before Sundays were computed, the empty list gave 22 March;
-- that expectation was changed with the rule, on the coordinator's instruction.)
-- Vintage: 22 March 2026 is before 26 March 2026, when the deposited Gov. Code § 6700
-- took effect; that Sunday 22 March is a holiday rests on that later text (NOTES.md, F9).
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 3 6) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 23
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 3 6) (LIST YMD 2026 3 22) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 23
-- Discovered Friday 9 October 2026: Saturday 24 October, so Monday 26 October; a listed Sunday 25 October changes nothing.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 10 9) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 26
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 10 9) (LIST YMD 2026 10 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 26
-- Discovered Friday 18 December 2026: Saturday 2 January 2027, so Monday 4 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 12 18) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 4
-- Discovered Friday 22 May 2026: Saturday 6 June, Sunday 7 June, so Monday 8 June; with Monday 8 June listed, Tuesday 9 June.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 5 22) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 8
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 5 22) (LIST YMD 2026 6 8) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 9
-- Discovered Saturday 7 March 2026: the 15th day is Sunday 22 March, so Monday 23 March.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 3 7) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 23
-- Discovered Sunday 23 August 2026: the 15th day is Monday 7 September; a listed holiday on it moves the last day to 8 September.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 8 23) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 7
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 8 23) (LIST YMD 2026 9 7) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 8
-- A listed date that is not the last day changes nothing.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 8 23) (LIST YMD 2026 9 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 7
-- Across the year end: discovered Sunday 20 December 2026, the 15th day is Monday 4 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to report to the Office` (YMD 2026 12 20) `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 4

-- In time on the last day; late the day after.
#ASSERT `did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 17) `no other holidays`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 18) `no other holidays`))
#ASSERT `did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 3 6) (YMD 2026 3 23) (LIST YMD 2026 3 22)
#ASSERT `did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 3 6) (YMD 2026 3 23) `no other holidays`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 3 6) (YMD 2026 3 24) `no other holidays`))
#ASSERT `did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 10 9) (YMD 2026 10 26) `no other holidays`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the Office of Emergency Services in time` (YMD 2026 10 9) (YMD 2026 10 27) `no other holidays`))

-- Through the exported question: a large developer's model lost control and killed; discovered 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `must I report this incident to the Office of Emergency Services, and by when` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 2) `no other holidays` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 3 17, YMD 2026 3 17
-- The same, discovered Friday 6 March 2026, no holiday listed: 15th day Saturday 21 March, last day Monday 23 March.
#ASSERT `must I report this incident to the Office of Emergency Services, and by when` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` FALSE FALSE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 6) `no other holidays` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 3 21, YMD 2026 3 23

§ `Section 22757.13(c)(2): the 24-hour disclosure`

#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `imminently` EQUALS `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `plainly` EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I have not discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`
-- Not limited to the developer's own models (F12).
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `someone else's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `imminently` EQUALS `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a model of a developer below the line` `a weights theft that injured` `imminently` EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a large developer's frontier model` `nothing happened` `imminently` EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `by the federal route` EQUALS `deemed in compliance with the 24-hour disclosure to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the chapter`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose within 24 hours under (c)(2)` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `discovered 31 December 2025` EQUALS `not covered, because I discovered the incident before the chapter took effect on 1 January 2026, for the 24-hour disclosure`
-- Both duties at once: the 15-day report is still owed when the 24-hour disclosure is (F4).
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the Office` `a large developer's frontier model` `a weights theft that injured` `imminently` `no other holidays` EQUALS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` OF YMD 2026 3 17, YMD 2026 3 17

#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` 24
#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` 23.5
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I disclose within 24 hours` 24.5))
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I disclose within 24 hours` 25))

-- Through the exported question.
#ASSERT `must I disclose this incident within 24 hours` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` TRUE TRUE `no model conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 2) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction`

§ `Section 22757.13(a), (c)(3), (f)`

#ASSERT `what must my report give` EQUALS LIST `item 1, the date of the critical safety incident`, `item 2, the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`, `item 3, a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`, `item 4, whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `is my report exempt from public records requests` TRUE

§ `Section 22757.15: the civil penalty`

#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a large developer's frontier model` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 1 TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` OF 1000000, 1000000
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a large developer's frontier model` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 3 TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` OF 1000000, 3000000
-- A frontier developer that is not large has the duty but no penalty under § 22757.15 (F1).
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a smaller developer's frontier model` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a model of a developer below the line` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a large developer's frontier model` `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours` 1 TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty only if section 22757.15 reaches a failure to disclose within 24 hours, and then only the Attorney General may recover it` OF 1000000, 1000000
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 22757.15` `a large developer's frontier model` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 1 FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I have said the chapter is not in force, or is preempted, as applied to me, for the penalty`
-- Through the exported question: revenue $500,000,001 is large, $500,000,000 is not.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be made to pay for failing to report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000001 `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 2 TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` OF 1000000, 2000000
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be made to pay for failing to report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000000 `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days` 2 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
